ur interesting and honestly  frightening set of powers and the  equivalent exchange that seems to go  hand in hand with them  you ask for one thing and she shall  grant it for you but then you need to do  three things for her in order to balance  the spreadsheet so to speak she's  effectively the means by which gone  makes a miraculous recovery during this  material and if that's all there was to  this encounter  then you'd be hearing a very different  song being sung by me right now but  thankfully there's much more meat to  this plot thread and one that leans  heavily into the themes of family and  abuse kilauea's character has been  exploring since the beginning unlike the  rest of his family kilowatt cares deeply  about his sister and will do anything  for her well-being reading through  flashbacks which capture the early  moments of their toxic familial  relationship altering alaka's treatment  are both harrowing  scary and emotionally powerful  particularly when we fully come to grips  with how they've been treating her all  this time  symbolically this is the most overt  defiance of his family's wishes kilauea  has performed thus far and it's for the  benefit of another again a terrific  contrast with the scared individual that  would be afraid to overextend himself  particularly evident in the first act  when confronted by his brother illumi  being the most evident of this and as  kilowatt to his face defies him time and  again in this arc it's supremely  satisfying and what's more is that  kilauea uses this relationship with  allocate to  outmaneuver and out think his oppressive  family aiding in his escape of the  compound on route to the hospital  housing gone  as mentioned above there are two  separate plot threads running side by  side here  and neither are connected until the very  very end of the story the first being  kilauea's rescue and ultimate delivery  of aluca to gohan's bedside to heal him  all the while running from  and the second is  once leorio arrives at the scene during  the q a for the chairman voting  situation he is the first to hop up to  the podium and asks a rather pointed  question towards  jing asking the very question we've  wanted to ask all along  why hasn't he even attempted to see his  son and unsatisfied with the answer  leorio unveils to us  and jing his nan type catching him off  guard with a massive punch of the face  this was and i cannot begin to express  how much love i had for it upon first  reading if this isn't one of the best  moments in the series i don't know  what is and this sequence pretty much  sets the trend in place for the rest of  this half of the story leorio plays a  leading role in injecting just the right  amount of heart and humor  into the story to allow me to enjoy the  rest of the material as much as i did  i mean lyorio's indifference to being  chairman at the hunter association  coupled with his preposterous popularity  cemented him as my favorite character in  this series  he's just so much fun and i'm not even  done talking about him in this section  yet  but first let's finish off kilowatt's  story with aluka  zorodik  [Music]  due to the flashback nature of alako's  ability illumi takes the initiative and  attempts to kill his brother  before he can make a wish with aluca  regardless of how i may or may not feel  about alako coming into the story her  involvement offered a great mechanism  that pushes kilauea and his family into  conflict  this arc pulled a lot of weight that i  honestly wasn't expecting with the first  being a terrific capping off to killua's  character arc  once a young man petrified by the very  sight of his brother illumi and now he's  strategizing to outmaneuver and defy him  at  every possible turn and not really in an  effort to affirm anything necessarily  about himself or to raise his own  standing  instead it is for the benefit of his  sister and his best friend in the world  this sequence from the car chase the  involvement of the butlers their  conflicting allegiances  and the strategy from kilauea employing  the hot air balloons all the while alaka  provides numerous instances of scare  and horror made for a brilliant action  sequence that had me captivated from the  beginning to the very end with of course  the clear highlights of this section  coming by way of any direct involvement  from hisoka  or illumi but perhaps most significantly  what i loved about this sequence was how  it highlighted the greatest strengths  gone has  his ability to make lasting and powerful  relationships with people his ability to  make friends with kilauea ended up  making the surge of power he gained to  kill pito  possible to return from and his bond  with lyorio had him in the running for  winning chairman of the hunters  association and would have given him the  power to dedicate all resources of the  association to his recovery  and all of this happens within the arc  we anticipate he will meet his father  someone that not too long ago lamented  overgone's reliance on his friends  citing that trait as a weakness in him  overall it's a powerful and satisfying  merging of themes  eventually killable reaches gone's  bedside and it cuts to leorio's  continued success in the race  and in the middle of another speech  where he expresses his concern  and sense of powerlessness to help gone  the young hunter barges into the  auditorium leading leorio to embrace him  tightly  this moment was so sweet that i actually  welled up a little bit and yes this was  the moment that got me emotional if you  commented that down below  congratulations you know me very well  this was exactly the sort of stuff that  i was missing from hunter hunter  kurapika layorio and kilauea made such a  brilliant team of clashing personalities  that once it became almost entirely  about killaba and gonz dynamic that very  dynamic became a little less special  which was a shame because  i do love those characters and while  kurapika isn't in this arc at all  the tone and power of this arc was  helped immeasurably by lyorio the last  two chapters where gon finally gets to  share more than a fleeting exchange with  his father is a fitting end to what has  been a long story told over the course  of 339 chapters  while i personally didn't like jing as a  person i don't think it was important  that i did or did not  and the final panels of gon's time spent  with jing focused not on jing's  happiness or their collective joy  together  though that is definitely present here  and there primarily what i felt this arc  focused on towards the end  was the wonder and joy gone feels in  that moment with his dad  he's achieved what he set out to do from  the very beginning and in a way  that's so cathartic and powerful and  emotional and brilliant to me  to open up a bit i've got a rather  complicated family history and it's one  that i've been  very conscious was painting my  expectations and reactions to most parts  of the story from the beginning when i  was  three years old my parents divorced  leaving me to bounce between homes as  they both wanted to be in my life  i didn't mind this at all and really i  consider my childhood to be a very  secure and happy one i was very lucky i  do however have a younger brother seven  years younger in fact  one my mother had with another partner  after and long story short he left when  my brother was just one year old  and to this day we've never seen him  again and growing up it sort of put me  into a  strange role something akin to half a  brother and half a father once i got old  enough and reading through this story  looking at what gone was going through  how he was feeling and what sort of  clumsy and unkind treatment ching placed  in front of him all because he either  didn't want to engage or was nervous to  invoke strong and personal feelings i  had regarding that situation in my real  life  so when i say that i loved hunter hunter  i'm not saying that just to appease an  audience i know  loves the series also i sincerely mean  it as it gave me an avenue to better  explore my own complicated feelings  surrounding my family's history and the  love i have for my brother  for outsiders looking in i think it's  easy to look at a situation like this  objectively and see it for what it is  but when people you love are involved  and  waters are muddied suddenly the right  choice of action isn't obvious and it  becomes a series of compromises and  trade-offs  hunter hunter explored all of those in  great detail through a variety of  different avenues coming to a head  during the traumatic and devastating  chimera ants arc and thankfully climbed  out of that despair and injected the  hope and optimism  i looked to these stories initially for  and so in an effort to subvert the genre  consistently  it for me managed to create one of the  most cathartic shonen moments i've yet  read through unlike other stories i  don't think hunter hunter is one that  can be fully captured and realized  without digesting at all  and while i'm aware that kurapika's  story continues on after this  the heart of this tale for me was gone  and to see his story meet a fittingly  heartwarming conclusion in a series that  has been described as  notoriously grim and incomplete was one  of the most beautiful surprises  i've ever received from a manga maybe  this story will continue maybe it won't  but whether it does or it doesn't has no  impact  on how happy i am to have read it and to  have shared it with all of you these  last few months  as always i've been told not mark i'll  see you all next weekend  thank you so much for watching  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

